From dd8f52e793a7a140ad2df3a577d6cb315d4a39c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poovendhan Selvaraj <poovendh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 15:25:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: qce: fix CCM AAD buffer underallocation causing wrong
 auth tag

The formatted AAD buffer allocated in qce_aead_ccm_prepare_buf_assoclen()
is too small. The allocation uses:

  ALIGN(assoclen, 16) + MAX_CCM_ADATA_HEADER_LEN

but the scatter-gather entry for this buffer is set up with length:

  rctx->assoclen = ALIGN(assoclen + adata_header_len, 16)

For assoclen=32 and adata_header_len=2, the allocation is 38 bytes while
the DMA transfer length is 48 bytes. The hardware reads 48 bytes from a
38-byte buffer via DMA for CBC-MAC computation, causing the authentication
tag to be computed over 10 bytes of uninitialized memory beyond the
allocation.

Fix this by using the correct formula:

  ALIGN(assoclen + MAX_CCM_ADATA_HEADER_LEN, 16)

which guarantees the buffer is always large enough for the full padded AAD
including the length encoding header.

Change-Id: I75ff191cdef45d9e2c324fb2dcb883bf10a0a413
Signed-off-by: Poovendhan Selvaraj <poovendh@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/qce/aead.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/qce/aead.c b/drivers/crypto/qce/aead.c
index ca47859acab9..3d0700f3c2c8 100644
--- a/drivers/crypto/qce/aead.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/qce/aead.c
@@ -218,7 +218,7 @@ qce_aead_ccm_prepare_buf_assoclen(struct aead_request *req)
 	/* Get the msg */
 	msg_sg = scatterwalk_ffwd(__sg, req->src, req->assoclen);
 
-	rctx->adata = kzalloc((ALIGN(assoclen, 16) + MAX_CCM_ADATA_HEADER_LEN) *
+	rctx->adata = kzalloc(ALIGN(assoclen + MAX_CCM_ADATA_HEADER_LEN, 16) *
 			       sizeof(unsigned char), GFP_ATOMIC);
 	if (!rctx->adata)
 		return -ENOMEM;
-- 
2.34.1

